/**
@page conventions Units, frames and conventions

@section conv_units Units

All quantities are SI throughout the public API:

| Quantity              | Unit  |
|-----------------------|-------|
| Lengths, positions, shapes | meters [m] |
| Angles                | radians [rad] |
| Young's / shear modulus | Pascals [Pa] |
| Pre-curvatures, curvatures | [1/m] |
| Forces                | Newtons [N] |
| Moments               | [N·m] |

There are no hidden unit conversions anywhere (no millimeter-scaled
outputs). `ctr::math::deg2Rad` is provided for convenience.

@section conv_q The joint vector

The 6-DOF actuation vector is

@f[ q = [\beta_1,\ \beta_2,\ \beta_3,\ \alpha_1,\ \alpha_2,\ \alpha_3] @f]

- @f$\beta_i \le 0@f$ [m]: linear retraction of tube @e i into the actuation
  unit. Tube @e i spans the arc length @f$[0,\ L_i + \beta_i]@f$.
- @f$\alpha_i@f$ [rad]: axial rotation of tube @e i at its base.
- Tubes are ordered **innermost first** everywhere (arrays, indices, matrices).

The telescoping constraints (inner tubes extend at least as far as outer
ones, with a 5 mm clearance) are enforced by CTR::solveIK when it steps β.

@section conv_frames Frames

The global frame sits at the robot base @f$s = 0@f$ with the backbone
initially along @f$+z@f$. All returned positions/shapes (CTR::tipPosition,
CTR::backboneShape, CTR::tubeShapes) are expressed in this frame, in meters.

The orientation along the backbone is carried as a unit quaternion
@f$h = [w, x, y, z]@f$ of tube 1's body frame; the backbone tangent is the
third column of the corresponding rotation matrix.

@section conv_state The ODE state vector

`ctr::state_type` is a 15-dimensional vector indexed by `ctr::StateIdx`:

| Indices | Meaning |
|---------|---------|
| 0-1     | Transverse bending moment of the assembly @f$m_{b,x}, m_{b,y}@f$ [N·m], tube-1 body frame |
| 2-4     | Torsional curvatures @f$u_{z,1}, u_{z,2}, u_{z,3}@f$ [1/m] |
| 5-7     | Twist angles @f$\theta_1 \equiv 0, \theta_2, \theta_3@f$ [rad] |
| 8-10    | Backbone position @f$r_x, r_y, r_z@f$ [m], global frame |
| 11-14   | Orientation quaternion @f$w, x, y, z@f$ |

@section conv_bvp The shooting vector

`ctr::bvp_type` holds the five shooting unknowns of the boundary value
problem in **non-dimensionalized** form (every component in [1/m]):

@f[ x = \left[\frac{m_{b,x}(0)}{EI_1},\ \frac{m_{b,y}(0)}{EI_1},\
u_{z,1}(0),\ u_{z,2}(0),\ u_{z,3}(0)\right] @f]

where @f$EI_1@f$ is the innermost tube's bending stiffness. A zero vector is
always a valid cold-start guess; passing the previous solution warm-starts
the solve (recommended for tracking).
*/
